[{:db/id "q-341981/field-1/906fb68e52f34c93aaa89471be2f2ff4994dc9adb32c934377257fa64a54e307" :answer/id #uuid "7e6547f3-a2fc-5780-9052-18f283aedd94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186289658 :answer-field/choices ["q-341981/field-1/906fb68e52f34c93aaa89471be2f2ff4994dc9adb32c934377257fa64a54e307"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342004/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer/id #uuid "2dd7e933-fcb7-5b18-952b-55e57545ab9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342004/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8166babf-0c39-5911-8ec1-c9b631a872b9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342004/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer-field/choices ["q-342004/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342004" :question/id #uuid "d3c1829a-8807-56ab-95ed-938993da9f28" :question/math-academy-id "q-342004" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-x+4, & x<1, \\\\ 2x-3, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3}^{1}(-x+4)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}(2x-3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+4x){|}_{-3}^{1}+({x}^{2}-3x){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =[\\,-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}+4\\cdot 1-(-\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{2}+4(-3))]+\\,[{4}^{2}-3\\cdot 4-({1}^{2}-3\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{2}+4-(-\\frac{9}{2}-12)]+[16-12-(1-3)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{7}{2}-(-\\frac{33}{2})]+6 \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{2}+6 \\\\  & =20+6 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342004/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342004"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-29739/selection/cd5e079fde19978562b84c87e245556b9d0b95f0bc7938117e3671aa3b7c0e08" :answer/id #uuid "7d112a57-0263-575c-ad33-496e425ab1a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29739/selection/3ecfc975b491d9d95179818d01cbe270cc6e504a74b30ee61d374b14e0de8442" :answer/id #uuid "ecbd94e8-0162-5a46-afb8-a1f117644bb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29739/selection/bc1aaa9670e8118cdb6ca0d3888d99928c842323e3d10885fe212d998358f89d" :answer/id #uuid "62743952-0366-51bc-aeca-cea3b44cf55d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29739/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" :answer/id #uuid "baba40d7-0ad2-5dde-9ccf-7de61d5c9aad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29739/selection/4147dfaaf1a0ee97173c2a46381e399703cca1c5b9760b15b5e30792f0b27acd" :answer/id #uuid "2c5c4ebe-ba72-5b6f-9790-2efac1eb642a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29739/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "721224c0-794a-527e-b70b-41b87069c5fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-29739/selection/cd5e079fde19978562b84c87e245556b9d0b95f0bc7938117e3671aa3b7c0e08" :answer-field/choices ["q-29739/selection/cd5e079fde19978562b84c87e245556b9d0b95f0bc7938117e3671aa3b7c0e08" "q-29739/selection/3ecfc975b491d9d95179818d01cbe270cc6e504a74b30ee61d374b14e0de8442" "q-29739/selection/bc1aaa9670e8118cdb6ca0d3888d99928c842323e3d10885fe212d998358f89d" "q-29739/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" "q-29739/selection/4147dfaaf1a0ee97173c2a46381e399703cca1c5b9760b15b5e30792f0b27acd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-29739" :question/id #uuid "f11a9469-77dd-5592-a5e2-e400aca2dd52" :question/math-academy-id "q-29739" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}, & x<1 \\\\ 6-5x, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}(6-5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})|}_{0}^{1}+{(6x-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2})|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{(1)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(0)^{3}}{3}]+(6(2)-\\frac{5(2)^{2}}{2}-6(1)+\\frac{5(1)^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}]+[12-10-6+\\frac{5}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-29739/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-29739"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-5047/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "21d0f3fe-8b92-5098-91da-33a897685f84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5047/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "65ce43a5-9fe5-5e24-aa7e-54696134f42d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5047/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "23adcbc2-3300-5708-b2e5-a73aa81573bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5047/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "cdb579d9-67a4-53cc-865b-a8c0296d2196" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5047/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "aecb74e4-a6f6-570f-8b69-14c38f61a0a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5047/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "952dc6b3-1e4e-5f19-8a10-ed619c78c640" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-5047/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-5047/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-5047/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-5047/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-5047/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-5047/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-5047" :question/id #uuid "b306839f-7159-5629-ab24-554eb2b191f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-5047" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{-5}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+2, & x<1 \\\\ 3, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-5}^{1}(x+2)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2x){|}_{-5}^{1}+3x{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{(1)^{2}}{2}+2(1)-\\frac{(-5)^{2}}{2}-2(-5)]+[3(3)-3(1)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}+2-\\frac{25}{2}+10]+[9-3] \\\\  & =0+6 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-5047/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5047"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-18004"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/d43fa0efcfb8788316c86958b1175741c136588e81a8119131d1ca0f8d8ee229.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of four line segments. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-316122/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "ac7443a1-00ce-54d3-9c5c-554d130cc1ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316122/field-1/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer/id #uuid "bd73cb7b-9901-5d6e-bba2-9419023d3ec0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316122/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4ea03e0-d23c-564a-ad66-b50e33e59bf0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316122/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-316122/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" "q-316122/field-1/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316122" :question/id #uuid "fa1ed858-bd59-5697-b4fd-680cbb34c192" :question/math-academy-id "q-316122" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/64ce1ae5f198ce41e55414d853b1bd99e73d747cddb80412b30246bfdb13a907.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Then,\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of two parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-3,1)$ and the line segment for $x\\in (1,4].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,= & {\\int }_{-3}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,= & \\,{{{\\int }_{-3}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}\\,+\\,{{{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,1).$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (1,4].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\, & =\\,{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =\\,8+6 \\\\  & =\\,14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316122/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316122"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338319/field-1/1114f773249b584f03ae90d8348b5b14abd566a3f244c0aad51e974a9460892e" :answer/id #uuid "a97442ad-2e34-5024-b4fb-63ff1e470729" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338319/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ad7120e-6272-51a0-92d0-34cc606a28d6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338319/field-1/1114f773249b584f03ae90d8348b5b14abd566a3f244c0aad51e974a9460892e" :answer-field/choices ["q-338319/field-1/1114f773249b584f03ae90d8348b5b14abd566a3f244c0aad51e974a9460892e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338319" :question/id #uuid "c7b9963d-ecf3-5165-a89b-7d1a2c7f953c" :question/math-academy-id "q-338319" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/82096496503c058ae31473029f7844ddff99fad024dd786c7bad88985279a9af.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Then,\n\n${\\int }_{-5}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of two parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-5,-1)$ and the line segment for $x\\in (-1,2].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,= & {\\int }_{-5}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+{\\int }_{-1}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{-1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {\\int }_{-5}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,= & \\,{{{\\int }_{-5}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}\\,+\\,{{{\\int }_{-1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-5,-1).$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-1,2].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\, & =\\,{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =\\,6+7.5 \\\\  & =\\,13.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338319/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338319"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338505/field-1/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" :answer/id #uuid "b2ccd115-b96f-51d6-8ec8-58d62e231313" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338505/field-1/96ee6a3361e9d457b88fc124f1f022ef8dc27c2272728293b480cef1fc3f4e34" :answer/id #uuid "132afdfc-3713-5399-8f49-101b47045d33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338505/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "60ec4486-a34c-5ab2-abb2-f87ce2c7f28c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338505/field-1/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" :answer-field/choices ["q-338505/field-1/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" "q-338505/field-1/96ee6a3361e9d457b88fc124f1f022ef8dc27c2272728293b480cef1fc3f4e34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338505" :question/id #uuid "0dd9a4c2-9470-5512-b36a-e625f617bf1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-338505" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/a1a419a984000b3b8559a19809416bcccc9eb8341985994c621c3a48d15109da.png)\n\nThe graph $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of three line segments. Then,\n\n${\\int }_{-5}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We divide the interval of integration into $4$ regions: the line segment for $x\\in [-5,-4],$ the line segment for $x\\in [-4,-3),$ the line segment for $x\\in [-3,0],$ and the line segment for $x\\in (0,4].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-5}^{-4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-4}^{-3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{4}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-5,-4].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,-3).$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{-3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,0].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $4$th integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (0,4].$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{4} & =bh \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3}+{A}_{4} \\\\  & =1-1+\\frac{9}{2}+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-338505/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338505"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117680/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "65edb11e-1e0e-5d4b-bc4d-5dbf5cafa493" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117680/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "9c2c7d95-276c-51d5-8e6e-1785b9a65df0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117680/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "213a9033-3c23-597e-a74b-6bf809abfba0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117680/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "1c8afb12-c143-5d6c-9273-ac8abd85f79d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117680/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "d68b4eca-f9a8-5f56-a553-5d20378e9e19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117680/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "98cde449-95b7-5409-84ce-9958ec24578e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117680/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-117680/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-117680/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-117680/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-117680/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-117680/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117680" :question/id #uuid "042f12f3-e4d4-5dee-9b70-77f357143515" :question/math-academy-id "q-117680" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/a433e9e9f2018c1f964f13b0ef248f72253f99f071f44e029c928598e9d04a32.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-4}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of two parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-4,0)$ and the line segment for $x\\in [0,2].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={{{\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,0).$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,2].$ The corresponding region is a square, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & ={s}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =8+4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-117680/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117680"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49215/selection/346bb843388553f663e7b0da28417e6456fd9ac830d17506e8a8505fa93b99bc" :answer/id #uuid "5c96d804-f537-52e4-b34d-fd4d435b98cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9-2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49215/selection/1a0d1ef44651dd8b07a38e864e0697ba93a13d037d30a3aa9239cdb80f1efde2" :answer/id #uuid "17280961-b8ed-5aa6-81f7-d8b50b1a9829" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11+\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49215/selection/b046eeef7e0af82ad274dc5622204d595b70285893c991958c42596a63f01003" :answer/id #uuid "7e76dd41-e945-5009-a407-63b8f134dd5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7+2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49215/selection/849788cf34787c3e1f98d01b3f6db7eccce146c8a45bdb3166ab3f6441ab3089" :answer/id #uuid "80b4f644-df23-51c0-8831-2901cfcbe042" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2+3\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49215/selection/99942423ae0c1eb071c3d8127501e58a527ed22962d2ad050204d16adb5c060c" :answer/id #uuid "ccc19608-29e4-5590-8c3a-58a595a50ab1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49215/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f394f966-6c73-55ab-af28-cd289c2d467d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49215/selection/346bb843388553f663e7b0da28417e6456fd9ac830d17506e8a8505fa93b99bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-49215/selection/346bb843388553f663e7b0da28417e6456fd9ac830d17506e8a8505fa93b99bc" "q-49215/selection/1a0d1ef44651dd8b07a38e864e0697ba93a13d037d30a3aa9239cdb80f1efde2" "q-49215/selection/b046eeef7e0af82ad274dc5622204d595b70285893c991958c42596a63f01003" "q-49215/selection/849788cf34787c3e1f98d01b3f6db7eccce146c8a45bdb3166ab3f6441ab3089" "q-49215/selection/99942423ae0c1eb071c3d8127501e58a527ed22962d2ad050204d16adb5c060c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49215" :question/id #uuid "ef200c23-7d18-56c9-a45a-07e8091b06fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-49215" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/11cf2a28b6ce6281de0299a4a585bc3c98bf891f6d958401f22aab2fc6ce5ef2.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of ${\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of three parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-4,-2],$ the arc of a semi-circle for $x\\in (-2,2],$ and the line segment for $x\\in (2,3].$  So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-4}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThe first integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,-2].$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =bh \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-2,2].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle of radius $2.$ Thus, we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe third integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (2,3].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid. Thus, we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2+4)(1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =6-2\\pi +3 \\\\  & =9-2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49215/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49215"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339677/field-1/f36060af683783fa259743cb7a8d7f930d693c18b3f7c57ecefa811d9acf58bb" :answer/id #uuid "9467e07b-6c43-5850-88f3-9487bfed200d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi}{4}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339677/field-1/5ee6516a6d088131eb24ae3dc04c7a4ef24ce726d69cbc8c9d47a4da3663b78c" :answer/id #uuid "8c5d5852-5bb2-560b-b2be-e53077c19cd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi}{4}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339677/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5093a3e2-4293-5880-96b6-2b9abe4fc11e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339677/field-1/f36060af683783fa259743cb7a8d7f930d693c18b3f7c57ecefa811d9acf58bb" :answer-field/choices ["q-339677/field-1/f36060af683783fa259743cb7a8d7f930d693c18b3f7c57ecefa811d9acf58bb" "q-339677/field-1/5ee6516a6d088131eb24ae3dc04c7a4ef24ce726d69cbc8c9d47a4da3663b78c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339677" :question/id #uuid "b7dbda93-ab32-56ef-a596-f9f3d692e6ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-339677" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/353412402972b390de950f56b3273d8dbecf60d4d07c7c27e9281c28145a86d2.png)\n\nIf the graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above, then\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of $4$ parts: the arc of the quarter-circle for $x\\in [-3,-1],$ the line segment for $x\\in [-1,1],$ the line segment for $x\\in (1,4],$ and the arc of the quarter-circle for $x\\in [4,7].$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}+{{{\\int }_{4}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{4}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,-1].$ The corresponding region is a combination of a rectangle and a quarter-circle of radius $2,$ so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =bh-\\frac{1}{4}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =(2)(3)-\\frac{1}{4}\\pi (2)^{2} \\\\  & =6-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=\\pi -6.\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-1,1].$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =bh \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (1,4].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+3)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $4$th integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [4,7].$ The corresponding region is a quarter-circle of radius $3,$ so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\pi (3)^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3}+{A}_{4} \\\\  & =\\pi -6-2+6+\\frac{9\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{13\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pi -8}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-339677/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339677"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-49176"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/83b23d8138091a931d14854b197752d25d8149ee8914a70b8db73b6c2369c888.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of \n${\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of $2$ parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-2,3)$ and the arc of the semi-circle for $x\\in [3,5].$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,3).$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =b\\cdot h \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot (1)^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =10+\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-49169/selection/d2d402cd89b594d41bcd11b129436a1a995bb32de4caeae5740c6c84c906bee9" :answer/id #uuid "d2e2c2f2-e28a-5f34-bf45-10f12eab567f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49169/selection/52ba3485d70f448921dfdaaa53f089f0a66aa0adc1adfadccd2986bc2a54c218" :answer/id #uuid "ff462772-7b83-513f-ad9d-8e4ef5d0f5f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi -6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49169/selection/6bfe5d8533b997e09c440749f165ca47e97eb156d9d2e03f5c85078d2a4d27c0" :answer/id #uuid "edf633c4-274b-570c-a0d0-b65c6697f23e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi -12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49169/selection/a2bc245c20b0c97392497e5370e0f23f805adff79f279a5ca63fc5663a1ce0ee" :answer/id #uuid "8115f8cc-a039-5bf1-84d4-8bb1b1d08234" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi +12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49169/selection/ccff642009651421f0aa5fc182805bbf8622b103377909a189d6ab0e476b5a2b" :answer/id #uuid "9d1aa191-05da-5e5a-8720-ea487550217e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49169/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da1d6452-abf2-58d9-9d50-98c6dad60827" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49169/selection/6bfe5d8533b997e09c440749f165ca47e97eb156d9d2e03f5c85078d2a4d27c0" :answer-field/choices ["q-49169/selection/d2d402cd89b594d41bcd11b129436a1a995bb32de4caeae5740c6c84c906bee9" "q-49169/selection/52ba3485d70f448921dfdaaa53f089f0a66aa0adc1adfadccd2986bc2a54c218" "q-49169/selection/6bfe5d8533b997e09c440749f165ca47e97eb156d9d2e03f5c85078d2a4d27c0" "q-49169/selection/a2bc245c20b0c97392497e5370e0f23f805adff79f279a5ca63fc5663a1ce0ee" "q-49169/selection/ccff642009651421f0aa5fc182805bbf8622b103377909a189d6ab0e476b5a2b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49169" :question/id #uuid "10eefb23-e667-5ee1-a761-4753001a7b4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-49169" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/555b702c1903f8cc4e379ad4281aa86708757755e4f9fb14b0ec7790a80a17dd.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of \n${\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of $3$ parts: the arc of the quarter-circle for $x\\in [-4,-2),$ the arc of the quarter-circle for $x\\in (-2,0],$ and the line segment for $x\\in (0,4].$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-2}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={{{\\int }_{-4}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,-2).$ The corresponding region is a quarter-circle with the radius of $2$, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-2,0].$ The corresponding region is a quarter-circle with the radius of $2$, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (0,4].$  The corresponding region is the trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2+4)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{3}=-12.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\pi +\\pi -12=2\\pi -12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49169/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49169"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-353387"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/877771be920838a330edabe84b07eb817f1f3d7f1343b6866b9c2f078e079a67.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of \n${\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-433"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/ad45cbdcd126df931f1a35c60ca12b45d520a2a0a5cddf4fa012c0515d3024c7.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Find the value of $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{4} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-434"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/36c6a1c84e0b0c32a5fd35fd422645f60340da6d205dd8cc31054cd558c2f5f9.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of $\\displaystyle \\int_{-4}^4 f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
